---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { team } from '../data';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About the DevNotes Editorial Team | DevNotes"
	description="Meet the developers behind DevNotes and learn how we research, write, review and update every guide and article we publish."
>
	<h1>About DevNotes</h1>
	<p class="lead">An independent publication by developers, for developers.</p>
	<img
		class="feature-img"
		src="/images/about.svg"
		alt="Three DevNotes editors reviewing a pull request together on a large monitor"
		width="960"
		height="400"
	/>

	<section class="prose">
		<h2>Our story</h2>
		<p>
			DevNotes began in 2021 as a private repository of notes kept by Ana Kowalski while she was
			onboarding junior developers at a small agency. The notes explained concepts the way she wished
			someone had explained them to her: starting with the mental model, then the syntax, then the
			edge cases. When colleagues started sharing the links outside the company, she published them
			as a website.
		</p>
		<p>
			Since then DevNotes has grown to a small editorial team and tens of thousands of monthly
			readers. We remain fully independent. Sponsorships are clearly labelled, never influence what
			we recommend, and never appear inside a guide.
		</p>

		<h2>How we write</h2>
		<h3>Research and drafting</h3>
		<p>
			Every guide starts with a question real developers ask. We read the specification and official
			documentation, build a small project that exercises the feature, and only then begin writing.
		</p>
		<h3>Technical review</h3>
		<p>
			A second editor runs every code sample and checks every claim before publication. Guides are
			re-reviewed twice a year, and corrections are logged publicly.
		</p>

		<h2>The team</h2>
		<ul>
			{team.map((person) => <li><strong>{person.name}</strong>, {person.role}</li>)}
		</ul>
		<p>Want to contribute or report a mistake? <a href="/contact">Get in touch with the editors</a>.</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
